README file is for the Virtuoso ADE Explorer and Assembler S2: ADE Assembler and Multi Test Corner Analysis 
using IC 25.1 Base and SPECTRE24.1 ISR6 This software will only run on Red Hat Linux 8.4 and above.
  
Course Developer: 

Sai Darshan S Nishani
Cadence Design Systems

Course Editor:
Karishma Choudhary
Cadence Design Systems

Software Required: 

The VAEAS2: ADE Assembler and Multi Test Corner Analysis Course requires the install of: 
    IC25.1 Base
    SPECTRE24.1 ISR6
    
Licenses:
    VSE L, XL
    Virtuoso ADE Explorer
    Virtuoso ADE Assembler
    ViVA 
    SPECTRE + tokens 

Course install:

Copy and untar the VAEAS2_IC_25_1.tar.gz (or.Z) database to the login directory (user30 or whatever).
In a Cadence classroom, you should automatically be changed to the VAEAS2
directory upon login. 

Environment setup:

A .class_steup file should automatically source the software in a Cadence onsite classroom.

For offsite classes, the VAEAS2 directory contains a cshrc file which
contains the variables:
CDSHOME pointing to the install directory for IC 25.1, and 
SPECTREHOME which points to the install directory for SPECTRE24.1
 
These paths will need to be modified
for the installed software, and added to the login cshrc file,
or sourced before starting lab.

source cshrc

Checking the install:

Run the .testscript file to properly test and install the 
course before teaching it. It should report PASSED
without any errors. The testscript only works if nothing has been
changed, such as paths in the .class_setup file.

Lecture Slides:

PDFs of the lecture slides can be accessed from the ESD homepage.
The lecture also exists as a PPT file.

Instructor Guide:

A detailed instructor guide is available to assist you in
teaching this course, which can be accessed from the ESD homepage.

If you have any comments or corrections on the course or the install
or problems with any of the labs, please let me know.

Course Developer: Sai Darshan S Nishani
